<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Kullback–Leibler divergence, used to constrain policy deviation.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.13.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Rollout policy for BAPO, which synchronizes to <math id="A1.SS1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> every <math id="A1.SS1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.14.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM policy parameterized by <math id="A1.SS1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.15.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Reference policy (e.g., initial pre-trained model).</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.16.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Importance sampling ratio: <math id="A1.SS1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\pi_{\text{old}}(y|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\pi_{\text{old}}(y|x)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.17.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Reward function, we set to binary (0/1) based on correctness.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.18.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Expected reward under policy <math id="A1.SS1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> for input <math id="A1.SS1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. We approximate this value using the mean of <math id="A1.SS1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="A1.SS1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> responses <math id="A1.SS1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the rollout policy <math id="A1.SS1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for each prompt <math id="A1.SS1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha,r,\varepsilon}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha,r,\varepsilon}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.19.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard deviation of rewards under policy <math id="A1.SS1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for input <math id="A1.SS1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, with smoothing <math id="A1.SS1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m35" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.20.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Expected reward of policy <math id="A1.SS1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> for input <math id="A1.SS1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS1.m38" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[r(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[r(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)\mid\mu,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)\mid\mu,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A1.SS1.tab1.1.21.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A sampling method that assigns weights to online rollouts based on a normal distribution centered at <math id="A1.SS1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with standard deviation <math id="A1.SS1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, used to filter samples by their group mean reward <math id="A1.SS1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha,r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Theoretical Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Kantorovich-Rubenstein duality of total variation distance)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Kantorovich-Rubinstein duality (variational representation) of the total variation distance is as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TV}(m_{1},m_{2})=\frac{1}{2L}\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{L}}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{Z\sim m_{1}}[g(Z)]-\mathbb{E}_{Z\sim m_{2}}[g(Z)]\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TV}(m_{1},m_{2})=\frac{1}{2L}\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{L}}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{Z\sim m_{1}}[g(Z)]-\mathbb{E}_{Z\sim m_{2}}[g(Z)]\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{L}=\{g:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathbb{R},\|g\|_{\infty}\leq L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{L}=\{g:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathbb{R},\|g\|_{\infty}\leq L\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Policy Improvement Lower Bound with Adaptive Training Batch</span>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume rewards are bounded: <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the current policy, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the delayed rollout policy, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the current policy for re-evaluation, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{3}=\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{3}=\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the buffer policy distribution, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the filtering function partitioning samples into <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}&lt;c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}&lt;c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. and the following TV distance constraints hold:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{1}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{1}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta_{3}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta_{3}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1},\delta_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1},\delta_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are sufficiently small such that the variance lower bounds remain positive.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for the policy update objective in Equation <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Formal Definitions ‣ 3 Method ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the expected policy improvement over filtered samples satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[I(x)(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]\geq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[I(x)(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]\geq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}}\left[L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}K_{i}}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}}\left[L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}K_{i}}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))</annotation></semantics></math>. The constants are:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the bound by analyzing each filtered sample set separately, applying off-policy policy improvement bounds tailored to the reference distribution used in each region.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Core inequality for off-policy samples.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we establish the fundamental inequality:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2K_{i}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2K_{i}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant that depends on the variance of rewards in each filtered subset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we expand the advantage objective. By definition:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\alpha_{i}(y|x)}A_{\alpha_{i}}(x,y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\alpha_{i}(y|x)}A_{\alpha_{i}}(x,y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\alpha_{i}(y|x)}\cdot\frac{r(x,y)-\mu_{\alpha_{i},r}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\alpha_{i}(y|x)}\cdot\frac{r(x,y)-\mu_{\alpha_{i},r}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we establish the key algebraic identity relating <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))+(J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))+(J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Application of Kantorovich-Rubenstein duality:</span> For bounded rewards with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r\|_{\infty}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r\|_{\infty}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the Kantorovich-Rubenstein duality Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Kantorovich-Rubenstein duality of total variation distance). ‣ A.2 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> provides:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x))-J(\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}=\frac{1-\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}{\sigma_{\alpha_{i},r,\varepsilon}(x)}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these bounds yields the desired inequality.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Analysis for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (Filtered fresh samples).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, samples are generated by the delayed rollout policy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=\pi_{\theta_{t-v}}</annotation></semantics></math> and selected via Gaussian sampling with group-level accuracy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)\in\{\frac{1}{G},\frac{2}{G},\ldots,\frac{G-1}{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)\in\{\frac{1}{G},\frac{2}{G},\ldots,\frac{G-1}{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, excluding extremes <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variance analysis on discrete set:</span> For the variance function <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p)=p(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p)=p(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> over the discrete set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\frac{1}{G},\frac{2}{G},\ldots,\frac{G-1}{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\frac{1}{G},\frac{2}{G},\ldots,\frac{G-1}{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimum value occurs at the boundary points <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{1}{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{1}{G}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{G-1}{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{G-1}{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, both yielding <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p)=\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p)=\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)=\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x))\geq\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)=\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{1},r}(x))\geq\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha_{1},r,\varepsilon}(x)\geq\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha_{1},r,\varepsilon}(x)\geq\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}=\frac{1-\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}=\frac{1-\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\frac{G-1}{G^{2}}+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Analysis for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (Re-evaluated difficult samples).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, samples are generated by the current policy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> through re-evaluation of historically difficult samples. The selection criterion ensures that historically difficult samples (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha_{B},r}(x)\leq c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha_{B},r}(x)\leq c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) now achieve improved performance (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}&lt;\mu_{\pi_{\theta_{t}},r}(x)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}&lt;\mu_{\pi_{\theta_{t}},r}(x)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>) under the current policy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since these samples are directly generated by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}=\pi_{\theta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the constraint <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}&lt;\mu_{\pi_{\theta_{t}},r}(x)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}&lt;\mu_{\pi_{\theta_{t}},r}(x)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> provides a natural lower bound, yielding:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{2},r}(x)=\mu_{\alpha_{2},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{2},r}(x))&gt;c_{1}(1-c_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{2},r}(x)=\mu_{\alpha_{2},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{2},r}(x))&gt;c_{1}(1-c_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha_{2},r,\varepsilon}(x)&gt;\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha_{2},r,\varepsilon}(x)&gt;\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving us:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}=\frac{1-\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}=\frac{1-\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{c_{1}(1-c_{1})+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Analysis for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (Historical high-quality samples).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, samples are generated by historical buffer policies <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{3}=\alpha_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{3}=\alpha_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha_{B},r}(x)\in[c_{2},c_{3}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha_{B},r}(x)\in[c_{2},c_{3}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\alpha_{3},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{3},r}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\alpha_{3},r}(x)(1-\mu_{\alpha_{3},r}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> achieves its minimum at the endpoints of the interval <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[c_{2},c_{3}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[c_{2},c_{3}]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{3},r}(x)\geq\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{\alpha_{3},r}(x)\geq\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha_{3},r,\varepsilon}(x)\geq\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha_{3},r,\varepsilon}(x)\geq\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{3}=\frac{1-\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{3}=\frac{1-\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}{\sqrt{\min(c_{2}(1-c_{2}),c_{3}(1-c_{3}))+\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 5: Combining the results.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Taking expectations over <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying the indicator function decomposition:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[I(x)(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[I(x)(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[\mathbf{1}_{\{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}\}}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathcal{X}}}[\mathbf{1}_{\{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}\}}(J(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-J(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x)))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbb{E}_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}}\left[L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2K_{i}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>TV</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbb{E}_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{i}}\left[L_{\alpha_{i}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x))-2K_{i}\cdot\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))-2\text{TV}(\pi_{\theta_{t}}(\cdot|x),\alpha_{i}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\pi_{\theta},\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All constants <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are finite, since denominators are strictly positive by construction and numerators are bounded by 1 under <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For binary reward tasks where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the contribution to the policy improvement lower bound is maximized when the expected group reward of the sample is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Recalling Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Policy Improvement Lower Bound with Adaptive Training Batch). ‣ 3.3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the lower bound for policy improvement on a specific data distribution involves the constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, which scales the penalty for policy divergence. The tightness of this bound is governed by the standard deviation of the rewards <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\alpha,r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\alpha,r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Due to advantage standardization <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}\propto\frac{1}{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}\propto\frac{1}{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, the effective step size in the advantage estimation and consequently the gradient magnitude is proportional to the inverse of the standard deviation. However, in the context of the lower bound analysis in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Policy Improvement Lower Bound with Adaptive Training Batch). ‣ 3.3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the stability constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K(\mu)=\frac{1-\sigma(\mu)}{\sigma(\mu)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K(\mu)=\frac{1-\sigma(\mu)}{\sigma(\mu)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where a smaller <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a tighter bound and thus a larger guaranteed improvement step.
For a binary reward function <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reward distribution follows a Bernoulli distribution with parameter <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(x)=\mathbb{E}[r|x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(x)=\mathbb{E}[r|x]</annotation></semantics></math>. The variance is given by:<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}(\mu)=\mu(1-\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}(\mu)=\mu(1-\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes variance, we take the derivative with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\mu}(\mu-\mu^{2})=1-2\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\mu}(\mu-\mu^{2})=1-2\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Setting the derivative to zero:<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-2\mu=0\implies\mu=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-2\mu=0\implies\mu=0.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since the second derivative <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\mu^{2}}=-2&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\mu^{2}}=-2&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, this is a global maximum.<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">At <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance is maximized (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.25,\sigma=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.25,\sigma=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>). This corresponds to the state of maximum entropy, where the model is most ”uncertain” about the outcome. Training on these samples provides the strongest gradient signal for distinguishing between correct and incorrect reasoning paths, effectively maximizing the information gain per step. Conversely, as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, causing the advantage estimates to numerical instability or the gradient signal to vanish. Therefore, selecting samples with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> theoretically offers the most efficient learning signal and the most favorable stability bound.<span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Online Filter Mechanism Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To investigate the impact of fresh sample selection on training stability and convergence, we conduct an ablation study using Qwen3 8B with a 4K response length limit. We compare three distinct filtering strategies for the online component (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mode 1 (Range Filter):<span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It retains samples with group mean rewards <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in[\frac{1}{G},\frac{G-1}{G}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in[\frac{1}{G},\frac{G-1}{G}]</annotation></semantics></math>. This effectively removes only the zero-advantage samples (all-correct or all-incorrect) that contribute minimal gradients.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mode 2 (Gaussian Filter):<span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A difficulty-weighted strategy that prioritizes samples with high variance (accuracy near 0.5) using a Gaussian distribution, thereby reducing the proportion of extremely easy or hard samples.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mode 3 (Uniform Filter):<span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A baseline that randomly selects 60% of the fresh samples regardless of their quality. This ratio was chosen to match the approximate data retention rates of Mode 1 and Mode 2 (approximately 40%–60%) for a fair comparison of data volume.</span></span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20722v1/imgs/filter_comparison_plot.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/182;" width="548" height="182" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span><span id="A1.F10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ablation on Online Filtering Strategies.<span id="A1.F10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Comparison of Range Filter, Gaussian Filter, and Uniform Filter on training stability (Grad Norm) and performance (Mean@8). The star symbol indicates the best checkpoint for BAPO.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The Value of Quality over Randomness.<span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> As illustrated in Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.3 Online Filter Mechanism Analysis ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, the uniform filter mechanism exhibits severe instability, characterized by exploding gradient norms and a complete collapse in performance after 150 steps. Since this strategy blindly includes all-wrong samples (where <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>), the model is forced to update based on low-quality, zero-advantage signals. Suppressing the token probabilities of incorrect responses without a corresponding positive signal introduces significant noise and uncertainty, ultimately destabilizing the policy. This failure highlights that the <span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">quality</span> of the training batch, particularly the exclusion of zero-advantage noise, is crucial.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Convergence Speed and Final Performance.<span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The Gaussian filter demonstrates faster convergence in the early stages. By focusing heavily on samples with the highest variance (accuracy <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math> 0.5), it provides the steepest learning signal initially. However, its final convergence performance is lower than that of the range filter. We hypothesize that the Gaussian filter restricts sample diversity by aggressively filtering out samples that are slightly easier or harder but still informative. In contrast, the range filter retains a broader spectrum of valid samples. While it learns slightly slower initially, it maintains a rich distribution of training data, preventing premature plateauing and ultimately achieving the highest asymptotic performance.</span></span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Training Dynamics and Test Curves</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in Figure <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.4 Training Dynamics and Test Curves ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ A.4 Training Dynamics and Test Curves ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we present more detailed training dynamics and test curves for the Planning and Vision Geometry tasks. The results indicate that both BAPO and DAPO consistently outperform GRPO in terms of training rewards. Interestingly, BAPO exhibits higher entropy, reflecting better exploration capability compared to other algorithms, which also results in longer response lengths.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20722v1/imgs/train_dyn.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/274;" width="548" height="274" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span><span id="A1.F11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Dynamics</span> during BAPO, GRPO, and DAPO post-training, including training rewards, training entropy, and response lengths.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20722v1/imgs/test_res.png" id="A1.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/135;" width="548" height="135" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span><span id="A1.F12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test Curves of Group Accuracy Changes</span> for mathematics, planning, and geometry tasks among AMC, CD-4 test set, and Geo-3K test set, respectively.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Computation Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.5 Computation Analysis ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we observe that BAPO’s computational overhead correlates with the number of samples requiring re-evaluation and the actual training batch size. For the Planning task, BAPO (w/o <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves the fastest training time by eliminating bad case re-evaluation, but this comes at the cost of reduced performance. For the Mathematics task, the high number of bad cases (as shown by the 0/8 accuracy samples in Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.3 Detailed Analysis ‣ 5 Results Analysis ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) means that under our re-evaluation frequency setting of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=5</annotation></semantics></math>, inference time exceeds that of GRPO. However, this additional time investment proves valuable, yielding better bad-case handling rates and overall test performance, as shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Results Analysis ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Table <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>. We plan to explore lower re-evaluation frequencies to assess the performance trade-offs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.375</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) runs significantly faster than BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>) due to the larger historical data volume in the latter configuration. This causes BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>) to maintain a larger effective batch size than BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.375</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>). Training logs also confirm this observation: BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0,c_{3}=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>) consistently utilizes 100% of the configured batch size (equivalent to on-policy methods’ batch size), while BAPO (<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.375</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0.375,c_{3}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) operates at approximately 70% capacity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="A1.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computational Overhead Analysis.</span> “<span id="A1.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Batch size</span>” <math id="A1.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the sample batch size <math id="A1.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and train mini batch size <math id="A1.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. “<span id="A1.T2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Time</span>” is measured in total training time (d=days, h=hours, m=minutes) on 8 A100 GPUs.</figcaption>
