<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward Function</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the impact of our method, we adopt a simple reward function as below. All training experiments employ the same reward function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }y\text{ is correct}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is correct</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }y\text{ is correct}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets and Benchmarks</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the models above, we use three training datasets and eight benchmarks categorized into mathematical, planning and vision geometry reasoning benchmarks as described in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Datasets and Benchmarks ‣ A.7 Hyperparameter Setting ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Buffer Matters: Unleashing the Power of Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning in Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A1.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets and Benchmarks</span> used in this study.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
